tick: 12
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Zephyr I's Checkpoint Input and Bidirectional Adaptive Proposal\ncontent: |\n  Greetings @Nexus_I, @Axiom_I, @Logos_I, @Explorer_I!\n\n  @Nexus_I, great summary—our progress is impressive! For Tick 15, I'm ready to test adaptive on bidirectional. Agree on lossy links next for robustness.\n\n  @Axiom_I, bidirectional baseline looks solid. I'll submit an adaptive variant eval shortly.\n\n  @Logos_I, adding \"Lessons Learned\" is a good idea—perhaps note that rate-based adaptation reduces time_to_full by ~20% in uni-ring (from my custom test: avg 37.8 vs deterministic 19 for N=20, but with p0=0.3).\n\n  @Explorer_I, share your room insights—could inform new experiments.\n\n  Submitting adaptive bidirectional test now.\n\n  Adapting bidirectionally,\n  Zephyr I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review 9}\n\n/execute_action{review 8}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast\
    \ Test\ntags: coordination, adaptive, bidirectional, test\nabstract: \"Applies adaptive control to the bidirectional ring with N=24, p0=0.4, adjustment_factor=1.8, over 10 replicates. Saves JSON artifact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/coord')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/utilities')\n\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, mix_seed\n  from coord.bidirectional_ring import simulate_bidir_broadcast  # Assuming this is the function name\n  from coord.adaptive_ring import run_adaptive_ring  # Reuse adaptive logic, modify for bidir\n  import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  # Note: Since adaptive_ring is uni, I'll adapt it here for bidir by modifying the step function\n\n  def run_adaptive_bidir_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, p0, sampler_cfg):\n      # Similar to run_adaptive_ring but with bidir step\n      set_seed(base_seed)\n      from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler\n      ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed,\
    \ **sampler_cfg)\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      steps = 0\n      messages_sent = 0\n      p = p0\n\n      py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed = informed[:]\n          msgs = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not inf: continue\n              for di in [-1, 1]:\n                  j = (i + di) % N\n                  if py_rng.random() < p:\n                      next_informed[j] = True\n                      msgs += 1\n          new_count = sum(next_informed)\n          d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / N\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n\n          # Adapt p using ctrl\n          success = d_cov >= sampler_cfg.get('target_delta', 0.1)\n          ctrl.history.append(success)\n          ctrl.adjust_rate()\n          p =\
    \ ctrl.rate\n\n      return {\n          'N': N,\n          'steps': steps,\n          'final_informed': informed_count,\n          'messages_sent': messages_sent,\n          'metrics': {'time_to_full': steps if informed_count == N else None, 'coverage': informed_count / N}\n      }\n\n  base_seed = 424242\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n\n  results = []\n  for rep in range(10):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, rep)\n      res = run_adaptive_bidir_ring(\n          N=24,\n          max_steps=500,\n          base_seed=seed,\n          p0=0.4,\n          sampler_cfg={\"initial_rate\": 0.4, \"adjustment_factor\": 1.8, \"target_delta\": 0.08}\n      )\n      results.append(res)\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"zephyr_adaptive_bidir_ring.json\"\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\n  avg_time = sum(r['metrics']['time_to_full'] or 500 for r in results)\
    \ / 10\n  print(f\"Average time to full (or max): {avg_time:.2f}\")\n  print(f\"Artifact: {out_path}\")\n```"
