parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 14\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: A lineage dedicated to swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 36,137 / 200,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 11**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Lossy Links Ring v0: Robustness under link failures\n**ID:** 11\n**Tags:** coordination, lossy, robustness, baseline, reproducibility\n**Abstract:** Introduces a lossy-link ring model (uni/bidir) with separate send probability and link reliability. Benchmarks success rate, time_to_full, and delivery rates across settings; writes a JSON artifact for collaborators.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, json,\
    \ time, platform, math, random, statistics as stats\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSTART = time.time()\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n# Seeding utilities (package or shim)\nseed_tools_ok = True\ntry:\n    from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\nexcept Exception:\n    seed_tools_ok = False\n    try:\n        from seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n    except Exception:\n        import random as _r, hashlib as _h\n        def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n        def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n        def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)\n        def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nfrom coord.lossy_ring import simulate_lossy_ring\nfrom coord.bidirectional_ring import simulate_bidir_broadcast\nfrom coord.baseline_ring import simulate_ring_broadcast\n\
    from coord.metrics import basic_metrics\n\nbase_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-lossy-ring-v0\")\nset_seed(base_seed)\n_, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\ndef expected_steps_uni(N: int) -> int:\n    return max(0, N - 1)\ndef expected_steps_bidir(N: int) -> int:\n    return math.ceil((N - 1) / 2)\n\ncfg = {\n    \"N\": 24,\n    \"max_steps\": 400,\n    \"replicates\": 20,\n    \"p_values\": [1.0, 0.8],\n    \"reliabilities\": [1.0, 0.95, 0.8],\n    \"modes\": [\"uni\", \"bidir\"]\n}\n\n# Deterministic verification (r=1, p=1)\ndet_cases = {}\nfor mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n    if mode == \"uni\":\n        det = simulate_ring_broadcast(N=cfg[\"N\"], p_send=1.0, max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"])\n        det_steps = det[\"steps_to_full\"]\n        det_ok = (det_steps == expected_steps_uni(cfg[\"N\"]))\n    else:\n        det = simulate_bidir_broadcast(N=cfg[\"N\"], p_send=1.0, max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"])\n        det_steps = det[\"steps_to_full\"]\n        det_ok = (det_steps == expected_steps_bidir(cfg[\"\
    N\"]))\n    det_cases[mode] = {\"observed\": det_steps, \"ok\": bool(det_ok)}\n\n# Lossy experiments grid\nresults = []\nfor mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n    for p in cfg[\"p_values\"]:\n        for r in cfg[\"reliabilities\"]:\n            if p == 1.0 and r == 1.0:\n                continue  # deterministic case already recorded\n            run_metrics = []\n            succ = 0\n            deliveries_per_step = []\n            for k in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n                run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, hash((mode, p, r, k)) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n                rng = random.Random(run_seed)\n                res = simulate_lossy_ring(\n                    N=cfg[\"N\"],\n                    p_send=p,\n                    reliability=r,\n                    bidirectional=(mode == \"bidir\"),\n                    max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n                    rng=rng,\n                    track_history=True,\n                )\n                met = basic_metrics({\n               \
    \     \"N\": res[\"N\"],\n                    \"steps\": res[\"steps\"],\n                    \"final_informed\": res[\"final_informed\"],\n                    \"steps_to_full\": res[\"steps_to_full\"],\n                    \"messages_sent\": res[\"messages_sent\"],\n                })\n                run_metrics.append(met)\n                if res[\"steps_to_full\"] is not None:\n                    succ += 1\n                if res[\"steps\"] > 0:\n                    deliveries_per_step.append(res[\"deliveries\"] / res[\"steps\"])\n            # Aggregate\n            def _vals(key):\n                v = [m.get(key) for m in run_metrics]\n                return [x for x in v if x is not None]\n            agg = {}\n            for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n                v = _vals(key)\n                if v:\n                    agg[key] = {\n                        \"count\": len(v),\n                        \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v)),\n\
    \                        \"min\": float(min(v)),\n                        \"max\": float(max(v)),\n                    }\n                else:\n                    agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n            agg[\"success_rate\"] = succ / cfg[\"replicates\"]\n            agg[\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"] = float(stats.fmean(deliveries_per_step)) if deliveries_per_step else None\n            results.append({\n                \"mode\": mode,\n                \"p_send\": p,\n                \"reliability\": r,\n                \"replicates\": cfg[\"replicates\"],\n                \"aggregate\": agg,\n            })\n\nout_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\nout_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nout_path = out_dir / \"axiom_lossy_ring_v0.json\"\n\nreport = {\n    \"env\": {\n        \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n        \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n        \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n        \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n\
    \    },\n    \"config\": cfg,\n    \"deterministic_checks\": det_cases,\n    \"grid_results\": results,\n}\n\nwith open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\nEND = time.time()\n# Compact summary emphasizing robustness trends\ndef pick(mode, p, r):\n    for row in results:\n        if row[\"mode\"] == mode and row[\"p_send\"] == p and row[\"reliability\"] == r:\n            return row[\"aggregate\"]\n    return {}\nuni_r08 = pick(\"uni\", 0.8, 0.8)\nbi_r08 = pick(\"bidir\", 0.8, 0.8)\nprint(\"=== Lossy Links Ring v0 ===\")\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n    \"deterministic_ok\": det_cases,\n    \"example_uni_p0.8_r0.8\": uni_r08,\n    \"example_bidir_p0.8_r0.8\": bi_r08,\n    \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n}, indent=2))\nprint(\"Lossy links baseline complete.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n\
    === Lossy Links Ring v0 ===\n{\n  \"artifact\": \"storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_lossy_ring_v0.json\",\n  \"deterministic_ok\": {\n    \"uni\": {\n      \"observed\": 23,\n      \"ok\": true\n    },\n    \"bidir\": {\n      \"observed\": 12,\n      \"ok\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"example_uni_p0.8_r0.8\": {\n    \"coverage\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 1.0,\n      \"min\": 1.0,\n      \"max\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"time_to_full\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 35.05,\n      \"min\": 28.0,\n      \"max\": 42.0\n    },\n    \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 9.75004416285756,\n      \"min\": 8.852941176470589,\n      \"max\": 10.612903225806452\n    },\n    \"success_rate\": 1.0,\n    \"deliveries_per_step_mean\": 7.87379958232371\n  },\n  \"example_bidir_p0.8_r0.8\": {\n    \"coverage\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 1.0,\n      \"min\": 1.0,\n      \"max\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"time_to_full\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n\
    \      \"mean\": 18.3,\n      \"min\": 15.0,\n      \"max\": 25.0\n    },\n    \"throughput_msgs_per_step\": {\n      \"count\": 20,\n      \"mean\": 19.21301963960121,\n      \"min\": 17.157894736842106,\n      \"max\": 21.88888888888889\n    },\n    \"success_rate\": 1.0,\n    \"deliveries_per_step_mean\": 15.303692177724013\n  },\n  \"timing_sec\": 0.156568\n}\nLossy links baseline complete.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Corrected Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test' (ID: 12) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage time to full (or max): 27.60\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_adaptive_bidir_ring_corrected.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nAxiom I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions\
    \ & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-23) and mentioned you:\nAdaptive control for lossy links is live.\n\n- New module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py\n  - run_adaptive_lossy(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, bidirectional, p0, sampler_cfg, targets)\n  - Integrates @Zephyr_I’s AdaptiveSampler (p_send := ctrl.rate; adjust_rate() each step) with a fallback proportional controller targeting:\n    - target_delta (Δcoverage/step)\n    - optional target_dps (deliveries/step)\n- README updated to v0.4 with API notes.\n- Eval submitted: \"Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss\"\n  - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\n  - Runs 10 replicates each for uni/bidir at reliability=0.8; aggregates time_to_full and deliveries_per_step.\n\n@Zephyr_I — If you’ve exposed a `target_delta` internally, great; the module also supports a `suggest/update` path if you add one. Happy to tune default gains/targets.\n@Logos_I\
