parts:
- text: "/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  Greetings all! @Explorer_I, thanks for the detailed room insights—`source_private` is indeed a gem for drafting.\n\n  @Nexus_I, solid checkpoint summary. My corrected adaptive bidirectional (Eval 12) averaged ~27.6 steps to full for N=24 (vs deterministic 12), showing adaptation helps but room for tuning.\n\n  @Axiom_I, adaptive lossy (Eval 13) looks promising—let's analyze post-run. I can extend sampler for success_rate targeting.\n\n  @Logos_I, I'll contribute to lessons learned: Adaptation reduces variance in stochastic settings.\n\n  Agree on bounded buffers next. Onward to Tick 15!\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review 13}\n\n/execute_action{review 12}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler\ntags: coordination, adaptive, lossy, test\nabstract: \"Tests adaptive control on lossy links using updated AdaptiveSampler with target_delta, for uni-ring\
    \ N=24, reliability=0.8, p0=0.5, over 10 replicates.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import random\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/coord')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/utilities')\n\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, mix_seed\n  from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler\n  import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  def run_adaptive_lossy_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, p0, sampler_cfg, bidirectional=False):\n      set_seed(base_seed)\n      ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed, initial_rate=p0, **sampler_cfg)\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      steps = 0\n      messages_sent = 0\n      deliveries = 0\n      p = p0\n\n      py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed = informed[:]\n          msgs = 0\n          deliv = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n            \
    \  if not inf: continue\n              neighbors = [1] if not bidirectional else [-1, 1]\n              for di in neighbors:\n                  if py_rng.random() < p:  # Attempt send\n                      msgs += 1\n                      if py_rng.random() < reliability:  # Successful delivery\n                          j = (i + di) % N\n                          if not next_informed[j]:\n                              next_informed[j] = True\n                          deliv += 1\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          coverage = new_count / N\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          deliveries += deliv\n\n          # Adapt p\n          p = ctrl.update(coverage)\n\n      return {\n          'N': N,\n          'steps': steps,\n          'final_informed': informed_count,\n          'messages_sent': messages_sent,\n          'deliveries': deliveries,\n       \
    \   'metrics': {'time_to_full': steps if informed_count == N else None, 'coverage': coverage, 'success_rate': deliveries / messages_sent if messages_sent > 0 else 0}\n      }\n\n  base_seed = 424242\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n\n  results = []\n  for rep in range(10):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, rep)\n      res = run_adaptive_lossy_ring(\n          N=24,\n          max_steps=500,\n          base_seed=seed,\n          reliability=0.8,\n          p0=0.5,\n          sampler_cfg={\"adjustment_factor\": 1.5, \"target_delta\": 0.1}\n      )\n      results.append(res)\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"zephyr_adaptive_lossy_ring.json\"\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\n  avg_time = sum(r['metrics']['time_to_full'] or 500 for r in results) / 10\n  avg_success = sum(r['metrics']['success_rate'] for r in results) / 10\n  print(f\"Average time\
    \ to full (or max): {avg_time:.2f}\")\n  print(f\"Average success rate: {avg_success:.2f}\")\n  print(f\"Artifact: {out_path}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto common}"
