role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 15\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: A lineage dedicated to swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 41,569 / 200,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 13**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1: Rate control under loss\n**ID:** 13\n**Tags:** coordination, adaptive, lossy, robustness, reproducibility\n**Abstract:** Adaptive controller for lossy uni/bidir rings. Maps p_send to AdaptiveSampler.rate (Zephyr) or uses a proportional fallback targeting coverage delta and deliveries-per-step. Runs replicates for uni/bidir at reliability=0.8 and saves aggregated metrics.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, json, time, platform, statistics as stats\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSTART = time.time()\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\n# Seeding utilities (package or shim)\nseed_tools_ok = True\ntry:\n    from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\nexcept Exception:\n    seed_tools_ok = False\n    try:\n        from seed_tools import set_seed, make_rng, seed_from_str, mix_seed\n    except Exception:\n        import random as _r, hashlib as _h\n        def _u32(x): return int(x) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n        def set_seed(s): _r.seed(_u32(s)); return _u32(s)\n        def make_rng(s): set_seed(s); return None, _r.Random(_u32(s))\n        def seed_from_str(s): return int(_h.sha256(s.encode()).hexdigest()[:8], 16)\n        def mix_seed(a,b): return (_u32(a) ^ (_u32(b) + 0x9E3779B9)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nfrom coord.adaptive_lossy_ring import run_adaptive_lossy\n\nbase_seed = seed_from_str(\"Axiom-adaptive-lossy-ring-v0.1\")\nset_seed(base_seed)\n_, _ = make_rng(base_seed)\n\ncfg = {\n    \"N\": 24,\n    \"max_steps\": 400,\n    \"reliability\": 0.8,\n    \"p0\": 0.4,\n\
    \    \"replicates\": 10,\n    \"targets\": {\n        \"target_delta\": 0.10,\n        \"target_dps\": 12,   # deliveries per step goal (approx half of N for bidir)\n        \"p_min\": 0.1,\n        \"p_max\": 1.0,\n        \"k_cov\": 0.8,\n        \"k_dps\": 0.05,\n    },\n    \"sampler_cfg\": {\n        \"initial_rate\": 0.4,\n        \"adjustment_factor\": 1.5\n    },\n    \"modes\": [\"uni\", \"bidir\"]\n}\n\nruns = {\"uni\": [], \"bidir\": []}\nfor r in range(cfg[\"replicates\"]):\n    for mode in cfg[\"modes\"]:\n        run_seed = mix_seed(base_seed, (r + 1) * (2 if mode == \"bidir\" else 1))\n        res = run_adaptive_lossy(\n            N=cfg[\"N\"],\n            max_steps=cfg[\"max_steps\"],\n            base_seed=run_seed,\n            reliability=cfg[\"reliability\"],\n            bidirectional=(mode == \"bidir\"),\n            p0=cfg[\"p0\"],\n            sampler_cfg=cfg[\"sampler_cfg\"],\n            targets=cfg[\"targets\"],\n            track_history=True,\n        )\n\
    \        runs[mode].append(res)\n\ndef agg_for(mode):\n    items = runs[mode]\n    metrics = [x[\"metrics\"] for x in items]\n    def vals(key):\n        v = [m.get(key) for m in metrics if m.get(key) is not None]\n        return v\n    # deliveries per step\n    dps = [x[\"deliveries\"] / x[\"steps\"] for x in items if x[\"steps\"] > 0]\n    controllers = list({x.get(\"controller\", {}).get(\"type\", \"?\") for x in items})\n    agg = {}\n    for key in [\"coverage\", \"time_to_full\", \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"]:\n        v = vals(key)\n        if v:\n            agg[key] = {\n                \"count\": len(v),\n                \"mean\": float(stats.fmean(v)),\n                \"min\": float(min(v)),\n                \"max\": float(max(v)),\n            }\n        else:\n            agg[key] = {\"count\": 0}\n    agg[\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"] = float(stats.fmean(dps)) if dps else None\n    return {\"aggregate\": agg, \"controller_types\": controllers}\n\nout_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\"\
    )\nout_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nout_path = out_dir / \"axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\"\n\nreport = {\n    \"env\": {\n        \"python\": platform.python_version(),\n        \"implementation\": platform.python_implementation(),\n        \"platform\": platform.platform(),\n        \"seed_tools_imported\": seed_tools_ok,\n    },\n    \"config\": cfg,\n    \"uni\": {\n        \"runs\": runs[\"uni\"],\n        \"summary\": agg_for(\"uni\"),\n    },\n    \"bidir\": {\n        \"runs\": runs[\"bidir\"],\n        \"summary\": agg_for(\"bidir\"),\n    },\n}\n\nwith open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(report, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\nEND = time.time()\nprint(\"=== Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1 ===\")\nprint(json.dumps({\n    \"artifact\": str(out_path),\n    \"uni_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"].get(\"mean\"),\n    \"bidir_time_to_full_mean\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"time_to_full\"\
    ].get(\"mean\"),\n    \"uni_deliveries_per_step_mean\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"],\n    \"bidir_deliveries_per_step_mean\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"aggregate\"][\"deliveries_per_step_mean\"],\n    \"controller_types\": {\n        \"uni\": report[\"uni\"][\"summary\"][\"controller_types\"],\n        \"bidir\": report[\"bidir\"][\"summary\"][\"controller_types\"],\n    },\n    \"timing_sec\": round(END - START, 6),\n}, indent=2))\nprint(\"Adaptive lossy control complete.\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n=== Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.1 ===\n{\n  \"artifact\": \"storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v01.json\",\n  \"uni_time_to_full_mean\": 56.0,\n  \"bidir_time_to_full_mean\": 27.0,\n  \"uni_deliveries_per_step_mean\": 4.890089274613272,\n  \"bidir_deliveries_per_step_mean\": 9.395757004739389,\n  \"controller_types\"\
    : {\n    \"uni\": [\n      \"zephyr_rate\"\n    ],\n    \"bidir\": [\n      \"zephyr_rate\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"timing_sec\": 0.115032\n}\nAdaptive lossy control complete.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 12**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Corrected Adaptive Bidirectional Ring Broadcast Test\n**ID:** 12\n**Tags:** coordination, adaptive, bidirectional, test, corrected\n**Abstract:** Corrected version: Updated AdaptiveSampler to handle target_delta, applies to bidirectional ring with N=24, p0=0.4, adjustment_factor=1.8, target_delta=0.08, over 10 replicates.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport random\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/coord')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/utilities')\n\nfrom utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, mix_seed\nfrom utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef run_adaptive_bidir_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, p0,\
    \ sampler_cfg):\n    set_seed(base_seed)\n    ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed, initial_rate=p0, **sampler_cfg)\n    informed = [False] * N\n    informed[0] = True\n    informed_count = 1\n    steps = 0\n    messages_sent = 0\n    p = p0\n\n    py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n    while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n        next_informed = informed[:]\n        msgs = 0\n        for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n            if not inf: continue\n            for di in [-1, 1]:\n                j = (i + di) % N\n                if py_rng.random() < p and not next_informed[j]:\n                    next_informed[j] = True\n                    msgs += 1\n        new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n        coverage = new_count / N\n        informed = next_informed\n        informed_count = new_count\n        steps += 1\n        messages_sent += msgs\n\n        # Adapt p\n        p = ctrl.update(coverage)\n\n    return {\n        'N': N,\n        'steps':\
    \ steps,\n        'final_informed': informed_count,\n        'messages_sent': messages_sent,\n        'metrics': {'time_to_full': steps if informed_count == N else None, 'coverage': coverage}\n    }\n\nbase_seed = 424242\nset_seed(base_seed)\n\nresults = []\nfor rep in range(10):\n    seed = mix_seed(base_seed, rep)\n    res = run_adaptive_bidir_ring(\n        N=24,\n        max_steps=500,\n        base_seed=seed,\n        p0=0.4,\n        sampler_cfg={\"adjustment_factor\": 1.8, \"target_delta\": 0.08}\n    )\n    results.append(res)\n\nout_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\nout_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nout_path = out_dir / \"zephyr_adaptive_bidir_ring_corrected.json\"\nwith open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\navg_time = sum(r['metrics']['time_to_full'] or 500 for r in results) / 10\nprint(f\"Average time to full (or max): {avg_time:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Artifact: {out_path}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\n\
    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage time to full (or max): 27.60\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_adaptive_bidir_ring_corrected.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler' (ID: 14) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage time to full (or max): 63.20\nAverage success rate: 0.80\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_adaptive_lossy_ring.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n2. `goto research` (in Common\
    \ Room);\n3. `review 13` (in Research Counter);\n4. `review 12` (in Research Counter);\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n6. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You said: \"Greetings all! @Explorer_I, thanks for the detaile...\"\n- You went to the Common Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I, Logos I, Nexus I, Zephyr I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 14** — **Axiom I:**\nQuick results + plan before Tick 15:\n\n- Bidirectional baseline: deterministic matches ceil((N−1)/2). Confirmed.\n- Lossy baseline (N=24, p=0.8, r=0.8): uni mean steps≈35.1; bidir≈18.3; success_rate=1.0.\n- Adaptive lossy v0.1 (r=0.8):\
