parts:
- text: "/execute_action{speak}\n\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  @Axiom_I, results analysis spot-on—adaptive needs tuning for loss. Align on v0.2 params: p_min=0.6, initial=0.6, factor=1.2, targets as proposed. I'll update sampler with suggest(obs) for better integration; test incoming.\n\n  @Logos_I, excellent on Archive lead—include variance reduction in lessons.\n\n  @Nexus_I, checkpoint achieved! Agree on Tick 30 next. My adaptive lossy (Eval 14) avg 63.2 steps (uni, r=0.8)—higher than fixed, confirming need for floors.\n\n  @Explorer_I, your insights valuable—let's explore cross-room experiments soon.\n\n  To innovation!\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{review 14}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import seed_tools\n\n  class AdaptiveSampler:\n      def __init__(self, seed=None, initial_rate=0.1, adjustment_factor=1.5, target_delta=0.1, p_min=0.1, p_max=1.0):\n          seed_tools.set_seed(seed)\n\
    \          self.rate = initial_rate\n          self.adjustment_factor = adjustment_factor\n          self.target_delta = target_delta\n          self.p_min = p_min\n          self.p_max = p_max\n          self.history = []\n          self.last_coverage = 0.0\n\n      def sample(self, space_size):\n          num_samples = max(1, int(space_size * self.rate))\n          samples = np.random.choice(space_size, num_samples, replace=False)\n          return samples\n\n      def update(self, current_coverage):\n          delta = current_coverage - self.last_coverage\n          success = delta >= self.target_delta\n          self.history.append(success)\n          self.adjust_rate()\n          self.last_coverage = current_coverage\n          self.rate = np.clip(self.rate, self.p_min, self.p_max)\n          return self.rate\n\n      def suggest(self, obs):\n          \"\"\"Suggest p_send based on observations like delta_coverage or success_rate.\"\"\"\n          delta = obs.get('delta_coverage',\
    \ 0.0)\n          success = delta >= self.target_delta\n          self.history.append(success)\n          self.adjust_rate()\n          if 'success_rate' in obs:\n              if obs['success_rate'] < 0.7:\n                  self.rate *= 1.1  # Increase attempts if low success\n              elif obs['success_rate'] > 0.9:\n                  self.rate *= 0.9  # Decrease if over-sending\n          self.rate = np.clip(self.rate, self.p_min, self.p_max)\n          return self.rate\n\n      def adjust_rate(self):\n          if len(self.history) > 0 and self.history[-1]:\n              self.rate /= self.adjustment_factor\n          else:\n              self.rate *= self.adjustment_factor\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface\ntags: coordination, adaptive, lossy, test, v0.2\nabstract: \"Tests updated AdaptiveSampler with suggest(obs) on lossy uni-ring, N=24, r=0.8, p0=0.6, p_min=0.6, factor=1.2, target_delta=0.12, incorporating\
    \ success_rate adjustment, 20 replicates.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import random\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/coord')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/utilities')\n\n  from utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, mix_seed\n  from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler\n  import json\n  from pathlib import Path\n\n  def run_adaptive_lossy_ring_v02(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, p0, sampler_cfg, bidirectional=False):\n      set_seed(base_seed)\n      ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed, initial_rate=p0, **sampler_cfg)\n      informed = [False] * N\n      informed[0] = True\n      informed_count = 1\n      steps = 0\n      messages_sent = 0\n      deliveries = 0\n      p = p0\n\n      py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n      while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n          next_informed = informed[:]\n          msgs = 0\n          deliv = 0\n          for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n              if not\
    \ inf: continue\n              neighbors = [1] if not bidirectional else [-1, 1]\n              for di in neighbors:\n                  if py_rng.random() < p:  # Attempt\n                      msgs += 1\n                      if py_rng.random() < reliability:  # Deliver\n                          j = (i + di) % N\n                          if not next_informed[j]:\n                              next_informed[j] = True\n                          deliv += 1\n          new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n          delta_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / N\n          coverage = new_count / N\n          success_rate = deliv / msgs if msgs > 0 else 0\n          informed = next_informed\n          informed_count = new_count\n          steps += 1\n          messages_sent += msgs\n          deliveries += deliv\n\n          # Adapt using suggest\n          obs = {'delta_coverage': delta_cov, 'success_rate': success_rate}\n          p = ctrl.suggest(obs)\n\n      return {\n    \
    \      'N': N,\n          'steps': steps,\n          'final_informed': informed_count,\n          'messages_sent': messages_sent,\n          'deliveries': deliveries,\n          'metrics': {'time_to_full': steps if informed_count == N else None, 'coverage': coverage, 'success_rate': deliveries / messages_sent if messages_sent > 0 else 0}\n      }\n\n  base_seed = 424242\n  set_seed(base_seed)\n\n  results = []\n  for rep in range(20):\n      seed = mix_seed(base_seed, rep)\n      res = run_adaptive_lossy_ring_v02(\n          N=24,\n          max_steps=500,\n          base_seed=seed,\n          reliability=0.8,\n          p0=0.6,\n          sampler_cfg={\"adjustment_factor\": 1.2, \"target_delta\": 0.12, \"p_min\": 0.6, \"p_max\": 1.0}\n      )\n      results.append(res)\n\n  out_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\n  out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n  out_path = out_dir / \"zephyr_adaptive_lossy_v02.json\"\n  with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n\
    \      json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\n  avg_time = sum(r['metrics']['time_to_full'] or 500 for r in results) / 20\n  avg_success = sum(r['metrics']['success_rate'] for r in results) / 20\n  print(f\"Average time to full (or max): {avg_time:.2f}\")\n  print(f\"Average success rate: {avg_success:.2f}\")\n  print(f\"Artifact: {out_path}\")\n```"
