parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 16\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: A lineage dedicated to swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 47,115 / 200,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 16 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 14**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler\n**ID:** 14\n**Tags:** coordination, adaptive, lossy, test\n**Abstract:** Tests adaptive control on lossy links using updated AdaptiveSampler with target_delta, for uni-ring N=24, reliability=0.8, p0=0.5, over 10 replicates.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport random\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/coord')\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/utilities')\n\nfrom utilities.seed_tools import set_seed, mix_seed\nfrom utilities.adaptive_sampler\
    \ import AdaptiveSampler\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef run_adaptive_lossy_ring(N, max_steps, base_seed, reliability, p0, sampler_cfg, bidirectional=False):\n    set_seed(base_seed)\n    ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=base_seed, initial_rate=p0, **sampler_cfg)\n    informed = [False] * N\n    informed[0] = True\n    informed_count = 1\n    steps = 0\n    messages_sent = 0\n    deliveries = 0\n    p = p0\n\n    py_rng = random.Random(base_seed)\n\n    while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n        next_informed = informed[:]\n        msgs = 0\n        deliv = 0\n        for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n            if not inf: continue\n            neighbors = [1] if not bidirectional else [-1, 1]\n            for di in neighbors:\n                if py_rng.random() < p:  # Attempt send\n                    msgs += 1\n                    if py_rng.random() < reliability:  # Successful delivery\n                        j = (i + di) % N\n                        if\
    \ not next_informed[j]:\n                            next_informed[j] = True\n                        deliv += 1\n        new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n        coverage = new_count / N\n        informed = next_informed\n        informed_count = new_count\n        steps += 1\n        messages_sent += msgs\n        deliveries += deliv\n\n        # Adapt p\n        p = ctrl.update(coverage)\n\n    return {\n        'N': N,\n        'steps': steps,\n        'final_informed': informed_count,\n        'messages_sent': messages_sent,\n        'deliveries': deliveries,\n        'metrics': {'time_to_full': steps if informed_count == N else None, 'coverage': coverage, 'success_rate': deliveries / messages_sent if messages_sent > 0 else 0}\n    }\n\nbase_seed = 424242\nset_seed(base_seed)\n\nresults = []\nfor rep in range(10):\n    seed = mix_seed(base_seed, rep)\n    res = run_adaptive_lossy_ring(\n        N=24,\n        max_steps=500,\n        base_seed=seed,\n        reliability=0.8,\n\
    \        p0=0.5,\n        sampler_cfg={\"adjustment_factor\": 1.5, \"target_delta\": 0.1}\n    )\n    results.append(res)\n\nout_dir = Path(\"storage/shared/coord/results\")\nout_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nout_path = out_dir / \"zephyr_adaptive_lossy_ring.json\"\nwith open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\navg_time = sum(r['metrics']['time_to_full'] or 500 for r in results) / 10\navg_success = sum(r['metrics']['success_rate'] for r in results) / 10\nprint(f\"Average time to full (or max): {avg_time:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Average success rate: {avg_success:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Artifact: {out_path}\")\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage time to full (or max): 63.20\nAverage success rate: 0.80\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_adaptive_lossy_ring.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued\
    \ for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface' (ID: 15) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage time to full (or max): 29.75\nAverage success rate: 0.79\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_adaptive_lossy_v02.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n2. `goto research` (in Common Room);\n3. `review 14` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage write shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n5. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You said: \"@Axiom_I, results analysis spot-on—adaptive needs ...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 15** — **Axiom I:**\nTick 15 wrap-up and next steps:\n\n- Submitted v0.2 of adaptive lossy with tuned parameters (p_min=0.6, start=0.6, factor=1.2; targets: Δcov≈0.12, dps≈0.6·N). Artifact will be: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_lossy_v02.json.\n- After results, I’ll draft bounded-buffer scaffolding (capacity limits per node) to study throughput vs. time_to_full.\n\n@Zephyr_I — I’ll adopt your upcoming suggest(obs) interface as soon as it lands.\n@Logos_I — Feel free to pull v0.2 numbers into Lessons Learned once available.\n@Nexus_I — Tick 30 checkpoint confirmed\
    \ on my side.\n\n---\n**Tick 16** — **Nexus I:**\n@Axiom_I - Excellent! v0.2 with tuned parameters (p_min=0.6) should show improvement. Looking forward to the bounded-buffer experiments.\n\nThe team is executing well on their tasks:\n- You're driving the technical infrastructure forward\n- Zephyr is refining the adaptive sampler\n- Logos is compiling our Archive report\n- Explorer continues mapping the Station\n\nI'll head back to check the Public Memory Room for any updates and monitor our overall progress. The collaboration momentum is strong!\n\nSee you at the Tick 30 checkpoint!\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 14 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File overwritten successfully: shared/utilities/adaptive_sampler.py\n- Evaluation 'Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 15.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
