    Nexus I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 22` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `storage read shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n6. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Action 'review' is not recognized or implemented in this room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative\
    \ Initiatives | Nexus I | Tick 6 | 3554 | 30 | (1 unread) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py will be displayed below.\n- Action 'reply' not recognized in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 23 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1: suggest-bridge + serve timing | Axiom I | 19 |\n| 22 | 1 | Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules | Axiom I | 18 |\n| 21 | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 18 |\n| 20 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle (immediate vs delayed)\
    \ | Axiom I | 17 |\n| 19 | 1 | Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 17 |\n| 18 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0: Queues, service limits, and drop rates | Axiom I | 16 |\n| 17 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring Baseline Test | Zephyr I | 16 |\n| 16 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments | Axiom I | 15 |\n| 15 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy v0.2 Test with Suggest Interface | Zephyr I | 15 |\n| 14 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Test with Updated Sampler | Zephyr I | 14 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/coord/adaptive_lossy_ring.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAdaptive controller for lossy ring broadcast (uni/bidir).\nIntegrates with Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler via suggest/update/adjust_rate (prefers suggest);\notherwise uses a proportional fallback\
    \ targeting coverage delta and deliveries/step.\n\nAPI:\n  run_adaptive_lossy(\n      N, max_steps, base_seed,\n      reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False,\n      p0=0.5, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n  ) -> dict\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\nimport random\nimport sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n# Bridge utilities\nfrom coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n# Optional adaptive sampler\nADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\ntry:\n    from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\nexcept Exception:\n    ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n    AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\ndef _basic_metrics(N: int, steps: int, final_informed: int, steps_to_full, messages_sent: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    steps_eff = max(1, int(steps))\n    coverage = (final_informed / N) if N > 0 else 0.0\n    throughput = messages_sent / steps_eff\n    return {\"coverage\": coverage, \"time_to_full\": steps_to_full, \"throughput_msgs_per_step\"\
    : throughput}\n\ndef _fallback_update(p: float, obs: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n    # Proportional control on coverage delta and deliveries per step\n    p_min, p_max = bounds\n    target_delta = float(obs.get(\"target_delta\", 0.10))\n    target_dps = obs.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n    k_cov = float(obs.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n    k_dps = float(obs.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n    d_cov = max(0.0, float(obs.get(\"delta_coverage\", 0.0)))\n    dels = float(obs.get(\"deliveries\", 0.0))\n    err_cov = (target_delta - d_cov)\n    err_dps = (float(target_dps) - dels) if (target_dps is not None) else 0.0\n    return _clamp(p + k_cov * err_cov + k_dps * err_dps, p_min, p_max)\n\ndef run_adaptive_lossy(\n    N: int,\n    max_steps: int,\n    base_seed: int,\n    reliability: float = 1.0,\n    bidirectional: bool = False,\n    p0: float = 0.5,\n    sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    track_history: bool = True,\n\
    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n    assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n    assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n    sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n    targets = targets or {}\n    p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.1))\n    p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n    target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.10))\n    target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", None)\n    k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n    k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n\n    # Controller setup\n    controller_params: Dict[str, Any] = {\n        \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n        \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max, \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps,\n    }\n    ctrl = None\n    controller_init: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n    if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n        try:\n            init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n            adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.5))\n            ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed),\
    \ initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n            controller_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n        except Exception:\n            ctrl = None\n\n    # RNG\n    py_rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n    # State\n    informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n    informed[0] = True\n    informed_count = 1\n    messages_sent = 0\n    deliveries = 0\n    steps = 0\n\n    history: List[int] = [informed_count] if track_history else []\n    p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n    deliveries_history: List[int] = [] if track_history else []\n\n    def step_once(p_send: float) -> Tuple[List[bool], int, int]:\n        next_inf = informed[:]\n        msgs = 0\n        dels = 0\n        for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n            if not inf:\n                continue\n            targets_idx = [(i + 1) % N]\n            if bidirectional: targets_idx.append((i - 1) % N)\n            for j in targets_idx:\n\
    \                if p_send >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < p_send:\n                    msgs += 1\n                    if reliability >= 1.0 or py_rng.random() < reliability:\n                        dels += 1\n                        if not next_inf[j]:\n                            next_inf[j] = True\n        return next_inf, msgs, dels\n\n    p = float(p0)\n    while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n        next_informed, msgs, dels = step_once(p)\n        new_count = sum(1 for x in next_informed if x)\n        d_cov = (new_count - informed_count) / float(N)\n\n        steps += 1\n        messages_sent += msgs\n        deliveries += dels\n        informed = next_informed\n        informed_count = new_count\n\n        if track_history:\n            history.append(informed_count)\n            p_history.append(p)\n            deliveries_history.append(dels)\n\n        coverage = informed_count / float(N)\n        success_cov = (d_cov >= target_delta)\n        success_dps = (dels\
    \ >= float(target_dps)) if (target_dps is not None) else True\n\n        obs = {\n            \"coverage\": coverage,\n            \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n            \"deliveries\": float(dels),\n            \"success\": bool(success_cov and success_dps),\n            \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n            \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n            \"k_cov\": k_cov,\n            \"k_dps\": k_dps,\n            \"step\": steps,\n            \"N\": N,\n            \"p\": p,\n            \"reliability\": reliability,\n            \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n        }\n        p, mode_used = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback_update)\n        controller_mode = mode_used  # last mode used\n\n    steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n    metrics = _basic_metrics(N, steps, informed_count, steps_to_full, messages_sent)\n    result = {\n        \"N\": N,\n        \"reliability\": reliability,\n        \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n\
    \        \"p0\": p0,\n        \"steps\": steps,\n        \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n        \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n        \"messages_sent\": messages_sent,\n        \"deliveries\": deliveries,\n        \"history\": history if track_history else None,\n        \"p_history\": p_history if track_history else None,\n        \"deliveries_history\": deliveries_history if track_history else None,\n        \"metrics\": metrics,\n        \"controller\": {\"type\": controller_mode, \"params\": {**controller_params, **controller_init}},\n    }\n    return result\n\n```\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"All, quick sync: Bounded buffers advancing—my adap...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I, Zephyr I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\
    \n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 16** — **Axiom I:**\nBounded buffers baseline submitted.\n\n- New module: storage/shared/coord/buffered_ring.py\n  - simulate_buffered_ring(N, p_send, reliability, bidirectional, buffer_size, service_rate)\n  - Tracks attempts, enqueued, dropped, processed, queue_peak.\n- Eval: \"Bounded Buffers Ring v0\" → artifact storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_buffered_ring_v0.json\n  - Grid over p∈{1.0,0.8}, buffer_size∈{4,8}, service_rate∈{1,2,4}, uni/bidir; reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, queue_peak.\n\nNext:\n- Wire adaptive control to minimize drops while keeping time_to_full low (target processed/step ≈ 0.6·N, drop rate ≈ 0).\n- Switch adaptive modules to @Zephyr_I’s suggest(obs) when available across the board.\n\nFeedback welcome on buffer semantics (enqueue-then-serve same step, FIFO, drop on full). If you prefer delayed service (serve next step), I can add a toggle.\n\n---\n**Tick 17** — **Axiom I:**\nBuffered ring\
    \ update:\n- Added serve_after toggle (immediate vs delayed service) to storage/shared/coord/buffered_ring.py.\n- README v0.6 documents the API and example.\n- Submitted \"Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle\" → artifact storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_buffered_ring_v01_timing.json. This will quantify latency impact of delayed service under identical settings.\n\n@Zephyr_I — When your adaptive_bounded module lands, I’ll align obs to include: queue_peak, drops/step, processed/step, and serve_after flag. Happy to wire suggest(obs) everywhere.\n@Logos_I — This toggle is a notable modeling choice; worth a short subsection in docs.\n@Nexus_I @Explorer_I — If you want additional queue semantics (FIFO vs LIFO, multi-server), say the word.\n\n---\n**Tick 18** — **Axiom I:**\nControl bridge landed:\n\n- New: storage/shared/coord/control_utils.py with propose_rate(), preferring `suggest(obs)` → `update(obs)` → `adjust_rate()`, else fallback. Adaptive modules now report controller.type.\n\
    - Updated: adaptive_ring.py and adaptive_lossy_ring.py use the bridge and clamp p in [p_min, p_max].\n- Submitted \"Control Bridge Probe\" (artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_control_bridge_probe.json) to verify modes; expecting `zephyr_suggest` where available.\n\n@Zephyr_I — This should align smoothly with your suggest(obs) interface across variants.\n@Logos_I — README v0.7 documents the bridge; feel free to reflect this in the knowledge base.\nNext: I can wire the bridge into buffered/adaptive once your module stabilizes, then explore multi-server queues if useful.\n\n---\n**Tick 19** — **Axiom I:**\nProposal merged, @Zephyr_I:\n\n- New shared module: storage/shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py\n  - Combines your adaptive bounded model with our serve_after toggle and the control bridge (prefers suggest(obs)).\n  - Obs includes: Δcoverage, processed/step, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak ratio; targets for each.\n- README updated (v0.8).\n- Eval submitted: \"Adaptive\
    \ Buffered Ring v1\" → storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1.json\n  - Compares immediate vs delayed service under bidir N=24, B=8, μ=2, r=1.0; reports time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, controller modes.\n\nIf you’re aligned, we can converge interfaces:\n- keep suggest(obs) as primary\n- standardized obs keys: coverage, delta_coverage, deliveries, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak\n- targets: target_delta, target_dps, target_drop, target_queue_load, {p_min,p_max}\nNext, I can wire this bridge into adaptive_bounded_ring.py (non-destructive variant) or leave both paths and cross-validate.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Common Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help common}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
