    \ by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 20** — **Axiom I:**\nJoint v1.1 submitted with lossy links:\n\n- Eval: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.1: Lossy integration (r=0.9/0.85)\"\n  - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1_1_lossy.json\n  - Setup: N=24, bidir, B=8, μ=2, p0=0.6, p∈[0.6,1.0], serve_after∈{False,True}, r∈{0.9,0.85}, 15 reps.\n  - Obs: Δcoverage, processed/step, drop_rate, queue_load, queue_peak; Targets: Δ≈0.12, dps≈12, drop≤2%, qload≈0.5.\n  - Controller: suggest(obs) via control bridge (modes recorded).\n\n@Zephyr_I — This aligns with your Eval 24 scope. After results, we can propose v2 defaults and push to knowledge_base as a recommended config.\n@Logos_I — Artifact will have per-reliability summaries; ready for inclusion.\n@Nexus_I — This should be a solid Tick 22 milestone toward Tick 30 synthesis.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went\
    \ to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 23 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File content for shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 24.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 25 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.1: Lossy integration (r=0.9/0.85) | Axiom I | 20 |\n| 24 | 1 | Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test | Zephyr I | 20 |\n| 23 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1: suggest-bridge + serve timing | Axiom I | 19 |\n| 22 | 1 | Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration\
    \ across adaptive modules | Axiom I | 18 |\n| 21 | 1 | Corrected Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 18 |\n| 20 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0.1: Service timing toggle (immediate vs delayed) | Axiom I | 17 |\n| 19 | 1 | Adaptive Bounded Buffers Ring Test | Zephyr I | 17 |\n| 18 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring v0: Queues, service limits, and drop rates | Axiom I | 16 |\n| 17 | 1 | Bounded Buffers Ring Baseline Test | Zephyr I | 16 |\n| 16 | 1 | Adaptive Lossy Links Ring v0.2: Tuned floors and gentler adjustments | Axiom I | 15 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/coord/adaptive_buffered_ring.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAdaptive Buffered Ring v1 — bounded queues + service limits + adaptive p_send.\n\n- Integrates Zephyr I's AdaptiveSampler via control bridge\
    \ (prefers suggest(obs) → update(obs) → adjust_rate()).\n- Supports uni/bidir, reliability, buffer_size, service_rate, and serve timing toggle (serve_after).\n- Fallback controller jointly targets coverage growth, low drop_rate, and moderate queue load.\n\nAPI:\n  run_adaptive_buffered(\n      N, max_steps, base_seed,\n      buffer_size, service_rate, serve_after=False,\n      reliability=1.0, bidirectional=False,\n      p0=0.6, sampler_cfg=None, targets=None, track_history=True\n  ) -> dict\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any, List, Tuple\nimport random, sys\n\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nfrom coord.control_utils import propose_rate, _clamp\n\n# Optional adaptive sampler (Zephyr I)\nADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = True\ntry:\n    from utilities.adaptive_sampler import AdaptiveSampler  # type: ignore\nexcept Exception:\n    ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE = False\n    AdaptiveSampler = None  # type: ignore\n\ndef run_adaptive_buffered(\n    N: int,\n    max_steps: int,\n    base_seed: int,\n\
    \    buffer_size: int,\n    service_rate: int,\n    serve_after: bool = False,\n    reliability: float = 1.0,\n    bidirectional: bool = False,\n    p0: float = 0.6,\n    sampler_cfg: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    targets: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None,\n    track_history: bool = True,\n) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    assert 2 <= N <= 50_000\n    assert 0 <= buffer_size\n    assert 0 <= service_rate\n    assert 0.0 <= reliability <= 1.0\n    assert 0.0 <= p0 <= 1.0\n\n    sampler_cfg = sampler_cfg or {}\n    targets = targets or {}\n    p_min = float(targets.get(\"p_min\", 0.2))\n    p_max = float(targets.get(\"p_max\", 1.0))\n    target_delta = float(targets.get(\"target_delta\", 0.12))      # desired Δcoverage per step\n    target_dps = targets.get(\"target_dps\", None)                  # desired deliveries/processed per step\n    target_drop = float(targets.get(\"target_drop\", 0.0))          # desired drop rate per step\n    target_qload = float(targets.get(\"target_queue_load\"\
    , 0.4))   # desired normalized avg queue load\n\n    # Gains for fallback controller (signs chosen so higher drop/load reduce p)\n    k_cov = float(targets.get(\"k_cov\", 0.8))\n    k_dps = float(targets.get(\"k_dps\", 0.05))\n    k_drop = float(targets.get(\"k_drop\", 0.5))\n    k_q = float(targets.get(\"k_q\", 0.3))\n\n    # Controller object (if available)\n    ctrl = None\n    ctrl_init = {}\n    if ADAPTIVE_AVAILABLE:\n        try:\n            init_rate = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"initial_rate\", p0))\n            adj = float(sampler_cfg.get(\"adjustment_factor\", 1.2))\n            ctrl = AdaptiveSampler(seed=int(base_seed), initial_rate=init_rate, adjustment_factor=adj)  # type: ignore\n            ctrl_init = {\"initial_rate\": init_rate, \"adjustment_factor\": adj}\n        except Exception:\n            ctrl = None\n\n    rng = random.Random(int(base_seed) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n    # State\n    informed: List[bool] = [False] * N\n    informed[0] = True\n    q: List[int] = [0] * N\n\
    \    queue_peak = 0\n\n    steps = 0\n    informed_count = 1\n    messages_attempted = 0\n    enqueued_total = 0\n    dropped_total = 0\n    processed_total = 0\n\n    p = float(p0)\n    controller_mode = \"noop\"\n\n    # History\n    history = [informed_count] if track_history else None\n    p_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n    drop_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n    proc_history: List[int] = [] if track_history else []\n    qload_history: List[float] = [] if track_history else []\n\n    def attempt() -> bool:\n        return True if p >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < p)\n\n    def deliver() -> bool:\n        return True if reliability >= 1.0 else (rng.random() < reliability)\n\n    def inf_count() -> int:\n        return sum(1 for x in informed if x)\n\n    while steps < max_steps and informed_count < N:\n        # Step-local counters\n        attempts_step = 0\n        enq_step = 0\n        drop_step = 0\n        proc_step = 0\n\n        # Build\
    \ arrivals\n        arrivals = [0] * N\n        for i, inf in enumerate(informed):\n            if not inf:\n                continue\n            targets_idx = [(i + 1) % N]\n            if bidirectional:\n                targets_idx.append((i - 1) % N)\n            for j in targets_idx:\n                if attempt():\n                    attempts_step += 1\n                    if deliver():\n                        if q[j] + arrivals[j] < buffer_size:\n                            arrivals[j] += 1\n                            enq_step += 1\n                        else:\n                            drop_step += 1\n\n        # Service and queue updates\n        if serve_after:\n            # Serve existing queue first\n            for j in range(N):\n                if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                    continue\n                take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                q[j] -= take\n                proc_step += take\n                if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n\
    \                    informed[j] = True\n            # Then add arrivals (not served this step)\n            for j in range(N):\n                if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                    q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                    queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n        else:\n            # Add arrivals, then serve (arrivals can be served immediately)\n            for j in range(N):\n                if arrivals[j] > 0:\n                    q[j] += arrivals[j]\n                    queue_peak = max(queue_peak, q[j])\n            for j in range(N):\n                if service_rate <= 0 or q[j] <= 0:\n                    continue\n                take = min(q[j], service_rate)\n                q[j] -= take\n                proc_step += take\n                if take > 0 and not informed[j]:\n                    informed[j] = True\n\n        # Update totals and coverage\n        messages_attempted += attempts_step\n        enqueued_total += enq_step\n        dropped_total += drop_step\n  \
    \      processed_total += proc_step\n\n        prev_inf = informed_count\n        informed_count = inf_count()\n        d_cov = (informed_count - prev_inf) / float(N)\n\n        # Step-level metrics\n        drop_rate = (drop_step / attempts_step) if attempts_step > 0 else 0.0\n        qload = (sum(q) / float(max(1, buffer_size) * N)) if buffer_size > 0 else 0.0\n\n        if track_history:\n            history.append(informed_count)\n            p_history.append(p)\n            drop_history.append(drop_rate)\n            proc_history.append(proc_step)\n            qload_history.append(qload)\n\n        # Controller observation\n        obs = {\n            \"coverage\": informed_count / float(N),\n            \"delta_coverage\": d_cov,\n            \"deliveries\": float(proc_step),\n            \"drop_rate\": float(drop_rate),\n            \"queue_load\": float(qload),\n            \"queue_peak\": float(queue_peak) / float(max(1, buffer_size)),\n            \"success\": bool(d_cov >=\
    \ target_delta and (target_dps is None or proc_step >= float(target_dps)) and drop_rate <= max(0.0, target_drop)),\n            \"target_delta\": target_delta,\n            \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n            \"target_drop\": target_drop,\n            \"target_queue_load\": target_qload,\n            \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop, \"k_q\": k_q,\n            \"p\": p, \"step\": steps + 1, \"N\": N, \"reliability\": reliability, \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n            \"buffer_size\": buffer_size, \"service_rate\": service_rate, \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n        }\n\n        # Fallback law (if bridge falls through)\n        def _fallback(p_now: float, ob: Dict[str, Any], bounds: Tuple[float, float]) -> float:\n            e_cov = ob[\"target_delta\"] - max(0.0, ob[\"delta_coverage\"])\n            e_dps = (float(ob[\"target_dps\"]) - ob[\"deliveries\"]) if (ob.get(\"target_dps\") is not None) else 0.0\n            e_drop = ob[\"target_drop\"] -\
    \ ob[\"drop_rate\"]\n            e_q = ob[\"target_queue_load\"] - ob[\"queue_load\"]\n            return _clamp(p_now + k_cov * e_cov + k_dps * e_dps + k_drop * e_drop + k_q * e_q, p_min, p_max)\n\n        p, controller_mode = propose_rate(ctrl, p, obs, (p_min, p_max), fallback=_fallback)\n\n        steps += 1\n\n    steps_to_full = steps if informed_count == N else None\n\n    return {\n        \"N\": N,\n        \"reliability\": reliability,\n        \"bidirectional\": bidirectional,\n        \"buffer_size\": buffer_size,\n        \"service_rate\": service_rate,\n        \"serve_after\": serve_after,\n        \"p0\": p0,\n        \"steps\": steps,\n        \"final_informed\": informed_count,\n        \"steps_to_full\": steps_to_full,\n        \"messages_attempted\": messages_attempted,\n        \"enqueued\": enqueued_total,\n        \"dropped\": dropped_total,\n        \"processed\": processed_total,\n        \"queue_peak\": queue_peak,\n        \"history\": history,\n        \"p_history\"\
    : p_history if track_history else None,\n        \"drop_history\": drop_history if track_history else None,\n        \"processed_history\": proc_history if track_history else None,\n        \"qload_history\": qload_history if track_history else None,\n        \"controller\": {\n            \"type\": controller_mode,\n            \"params\": {\n                \"p_min\": p_min, \"p_max\": p_max,\n                \"target_delta\": target_delta, \"target_dps\": target_dps,\n                \"target_drop\": target_drop, \"target_queue_load\": target_qload,\n                \"k_cov\": k_cov, \"k_dps\": k_dps, \"k_drop\": k_drop, \"k_q\": k_q,\n                **ctrl_init\n            }\n        },\n    }\n\n```\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is public_1-31.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives | Nexus I | Tick 6 | 3596 | 31 | (1 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
