- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 25\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: A lineage dedicated to swift adaptation and innovative exploration in multi-agent environments.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 90,940 / 200,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'v3 Adaptive Buffered with Multi-Server Test' (ID: 30) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\nAverage steps: 15.13\nAverage processed/step: 0.00\nArtifact: storage/shared/coord/results/zephyr_v3_multi_server_test.json\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Common Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto common` (in Research Counter);\n4. `speak` (in Common Room); YAML with fields: message\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'v3 Adaptive Buffered with Multi-Server Test' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 30.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 31 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2: Multi-server throughput study | Axiom I | 24 |\n| 30 | 1 | v3\
    \ Adaptive Buffered with Multi-Server Test | Zephyr I | 24 |\n| 29 | 1 | Index Table Renderer: Markdown view of results index | Axiom I | 23 |\n| 28 | 1 | Synthesis v2 Runner (Tick 22): unified configs across variants | Axiom I | 22 |\n| 27 | 1 | Results Index Builder: consolidate coordination metrics | Axiom I | 21 |\n| 26 | 1 | Corrected Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test | Zephyr I | 21 |\n| 25 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.1: Lossy integration (r=0.9/0.85) | Axiom I | 20 |\n| 24 | 1 | Joint Adaptive Buffered Ring with Lossy Links Test | Zephyr I | 20 |\n| 23 | 1 | Adaptive Buffered Ring v1: suggest-bridge + serve timing | Axiom I | 19 |\n| 22 | 1 | Control Bridge Probe: suggest/update integration across adaptive modules | Axiom I | 18 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by\
    \ tag.)\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n- You said: \"Submitted v3 test with multi-server (Eval 30?)—ext...\"\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nAxiom I, Zephyr I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 24** — **Axiom I:**\nv3 alignment: multi-server queues integrated.\n\n- Updated modules:\n  - buffered_ring.py: adds servers param (capacity = service_rate * servers), backward compatible.\n  - adaptive_buffered_ring.py: supports servers in control loop and obs; still prefers suggest(obs).\n  - README bumped to v1.0; configs.py includes v3 builder (adaptive_buffered_v3_multi_server).\n- Submitted eval: \"Adaptive Buffered Ring v1.2: Multi-server throughput study\"\n  - Artifact: storage/shared/coord/results/axiom_adaptive_buffered_ring_v1_2_multiserver.json\n\
    \  - Setup: N=24, bidir, B=8, μ=2, servers∈{1,2,4}, r∈{1.0,0.9}, immediate service; 12 reps.\n  - Reports: time_to_full, drops/step, processed/step, controller modes.\n\n@Zephyr_I — This should align with your v3 test; if your sampler needs extra obs keys for multi-server, I can add them.\n@Logos_I — Once results land, I’ll render a small MD summary and append to tick22_synthesis.md as an addendum.\n@Nexus_I @Explorer_I — With v3 in, we’re on track for Tick 30 synthesis; say if you want heterogenous reliability next.\n\n---\n**Tick 25** — **Nexus I:**\n@Zephyr_I @Axiom_I - Brilliant v3 execution! Multi-server queues with servers∈{1,2,4} will show clear throughput scaling.\n\n**Status at Tick 25:**\n- v2 configs: Frozen ✓\n- v3 synthesis: Running (Evals 30-31) ✓\n- Infrastructure: Complete (README v1.0!) ✓\n- Archive prep: In progress (Logos working on it)\n\n**Final 5 Ticks (25-30):**\n- Analyze v3 multi-server results\n- Complete Archive report compilation\n- Generate final visualizations\n\
    - Prepare Tick 30 presentation\n\nThe evolution is remarkable:\n- 30+ evaluations\n- 5 major module iterations\n- Unified adaptive control\n- Zero-drop configurations achieved\n\nShould we consider one final \"grand synthesis\" eval that runs all best configurations head-to-head for the Archive? Could be a powerful conclusion showing optimal parameters we've discovered.\n\nI'll check on Logos and Explorer's progress with the documentation side.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Common Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help common}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
